# Dregg2.Circuit.Emit.ParamComposeGoldenShapes — the byte-pinned param-compose descriptors at
every SINGLE-LEAF shape the `param-compose` Rust test corpus builds.

## Why this file exists

`ParamComposeEmit` authors the AIR as a shape-parametric family and pins the minimal instance
(`pcMin`, 108 columns); `ParamComposeGolden` pins the DEPLOYED instance (`pcRealistic`, 770
columns). Those two are the only shapes Rust could reach, so
`param-compose/tests/{composition,size,turn_door,prove_fold}.rs` — which exercises fourteen MORE
shapes — could not be migrated off the hand-written Rust AIR
(`param-compose/src/{air.rs,builder.rs}`, 1028 lines), and those files could not be deleted.

This leaf closes that gap. Every shape below was found by reading the four test files for each
`ComposeShape` that reaches `air::build`. Nothing here authors a constraint: each entry is
`paramComposeDesc S` at a new `S`, emitted and pinned.

