## Two shapes the tests build only to WATCH REFUSED, and are deliberately NOT pinned

  * `n1 p4 l3 k2` (`composition.rs::a_composition_over_a_shape_bound_is_refused`) — the refusal is
    a WITNESS property (a 2-subject composition over a 1-subject bound), raised before any
    descriptor is emitted. The descriptor at that shape exists and is uninteresting; the tooth is
    in the witness admitter, not the AIR.
  * `n4 p8 l8 k6 i31` (`size.rs::an_identity_width_that_would_go_vacuous_is_refused`) — the refusal
    is a SHAPE-GUARD property. `31 > MAX_SOUND_IDENTITY_BITS = 28`, so
    `ComposeShape.identityBitsSound` is FALSE and the shape must never be built. Pinning its wire
    would be pinning an object that must not exist. The `#guard`s below are the positive half of
    that guard; `ParamComposeRefine`'s vacuity teeth are the negative half.

## The structural cross-check against the Rust AIR being retired

`param-compose/src/lib.rs` publishes a MEASURED budget table for the hand-written Rust AIR
(`prog`, its own column count):

    n2 p2 l1 k1  ->  219        n3 p4 l3 k2  ->  379        n4 p8 l8 k6  ->  803

The Lean family emits 186 / 346 / 770 at those same shapes — **exactly 33 fewer at every one**.
That 33 is not a fudge; it is `param-compose/src/air.rs:312`'s single `zero` column plus the four
8-felt IV column groups `air.rs::wide_chain` allocates once per chain (`1 + 4 x 8 = 33`), which
`ParamComposeEmit` deliberately replaces with literal constants.

State the resolution honestly. Both terms are read off the Rust source and depend on NOTHING but
"there is one `zero` column and there are four chains" — no `n`, `p`, `l`, `k` or `ib` appears in
either — so `rust_prog(S) = leanWidth(S) + 33` is DERIVED shape-invariantly, and it is MEASURED at
the three shapes `lib.rs` publishes (two of which are in this file: `n2 p2 l1 k1` -> 186 + 33 = 219
and `n3 p4 l3 k2` -> 346 + 33 = 379). At the other twelve shapes here it is a derivation, not a
measurement. It is CHECKABLE at nine of them without new code: `size.rs`'s census and identity
sweep print the Rust `prog` at `n2 p2 l1 k1`, `n3 p4 l3 k2`, `n4 p8 l8 k6` and that last shape's
ib = 12/16/20/24, and `ParamComposeGoldenCensus`'s two shapes. What the constant delta buys is the
structural evidence that the emitted object is the same AIR gate family for gate family — it does
not, on its own, say anything about what either object MEANS. That is `ParamComposeRefine`.

## Axiom hygiene

Definitional instances + `emitVmJson2` byte-pin `#guard`s + shape `#guard`s. No theorem, no
`sorry`, no axiom. NEW file; imports read-only.
-/
